imx585-rpi-dkms (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Clear HDR, no longer experimental:
    - Output 12-bit companded data, which libcamera 0.8.0 expands back
      to linear. Highlights no longer render black.
    - Drop 16-bit Clear HDR mode. ccmp overlay param is now ignored.
    - Reach 4K 30 fps on 4 lanes at default link frequency.
    - Use high gain data in shadows for lower noise.
    - Limit gain by gain adder and round shutter to multiple of 4.
  * Hold exposure steady when frame length changes.
  * Fix lost rows in 12-bit modes at short line times.
  * Default overlay to 2 lanes, add 4lane param for 4-lane ports.
    2lane param is now ignored.
  * Set overlay rotation to 180 and orientation to external, matching
    Kurokesu module mount. Images are upright without app-side rotation.
  * Rename setup.sh to install.sh, setup.sh still runs it. Add
    uninstall.sh to remove a source install.
  * Break libcamera-ipa older than 0.8.0, which cannot expand Clear HDR
    data.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:44:40 +0200

imx585-rpi-dkms (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Quiet routine register writes and timing updates to debug level.
  * Report driver version in modinfo.
  * Stop leaving a build directory in the installed source tree.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:38:27 +0300

imx585-rpi-dkms (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Report crop rectangles in native pixel array coordinates.
  * Report full pixel array crop for binned mode.
  * Strip optical black rows from output with WINMODE crop.
  * Add 10-bit 4K all-pixel mode.
  * Rename HDR gradation controls, old names collided at 31 characters.
  * Clear HDR, now marked experimental and not yet tuned:
    - Add ccmp overlay param for 12-bit compressed output.
    - Offer 12-bit at 4K only, sensor lacks binned 12-bit HDR.
    - Fix register defaults against Sony application note.
    - Fix frame rate limits with a per-mode minimum line period.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:26:51 +0300

imx585-rpi-dkms (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release as a DKMS source package.
  * Driver state at this release:
    - 3856x2180 at up to 60 fps (4-lane, 12-bit), 10-bit and 12-bit
      RAW output.
    - 2-lane and 4-lane MIPI CSI-2 at up to 1782 Mbps per lane.
    - ClearHDR mode for high dynamic range capture.
    - Mono sensor variant support.
    - Three sync modes for multi-camera setups.
    - imx585 device tree overlay with cam0, 2lane, mono, always-on,
      link-frequency and sync-mode options.
    - Targeting Linux kernel 6.12 or newer.
    - Validated on Raspberry Pi 4 and 5, Raspberry Pi OS Bookworm
      and Trixie.

 -- Danius Kalvaitis <danius@kurokesu.com>  Thu, 02 Jul 2026 21:52:00 +0300
